        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix: isolate interactive PATH probes from caller terminal",
        "body": "## Summary\n- Launch interactive PATH probes in a detached session so shell startup cannot take ownership of the caller's controlling terminal.\n- Preserve process-group cleanup for timed-out and background shell children; the session leader remains the cleanup group leader.\n- Check spawn-attribute setup, cover the detached-session flag contract, and document the user-visible fix.\n\n## Validation\n- Exact head: `b1c9a5de6c834191b1b270e49ae2ad4869722a3f` (rebased onto current `main`).\n- Focused detached-session suite passes on macOS; Linux coverage now verifies both the libc-specific flag value and a real spawned probe becoming its own session leader.\n- `make check`: SwiftFormat and SwiftLint clean.\n- Autoreview: clean, no accepted/actionable findings; 0.95 correctness confidence.\n- Real controlling-PTY proof through public `ShellCommandLocator.commandV`: a hostile shell helper that opens `/dev/tty` was detached into a new session and could not acquire the caller terminal, while a normal interactive zsh lookup still resolved `/bin/sh`; foreground group `2092` remained unchanged.\n- Exact-head GitHub Actions covers both Linux architectures plus both macOS test shards.\n\n## Risk\nThe change is limited to shell PATH probing. Detached probes still run interactive login-shell initialization, but intentionally have no controlling terminal; terminal-dependent startup prompts can no longer interfere with the caller. Existing noninteractive CI behavior is preserved.\n\n## Dependencies\nNo dependency changes; freshness review not applicable.\n",
